                              CRITICAL INTEGRATION NOTES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

🔴 THREAD SAFETY REQUIREMENTS:
All governance components must use:
- ConcurrentHashMap for proposal storage
- ReentrantReadWriteLock for vote counting
- AtomicLong for vote tracking
- Synchronized blocks for state transitions

🔴 TRANSACTION ORDERING:
ProposalExecutor must respect dependency order:
1. Sanction enforcement (if any)
2. Reserve changes (if required)
3. Economic policy updates
4. Token minting adjustments
5. State synchronization

🔴 ROLLBACK SUPPORT:
If proposal execution fails mid-way:
1. StateManager.rollbackToCheckpoint()
2. GovernanceAuditLog.recordFailure()
3. VotingDAO.markProposalFailed()
4. Refund any spent gas/fees

🔴 SHARD COORDINATION:
For cross-shard proposals, ContinentalDAO must:
1. Collect votes from all 20 shards via RelayChainProtocol
2. Aggregate using ShardCoordinator
3. Execute atomically across all shards
4. Rollback all shards if any fails

🔴 EMERGENCY OVERRIDE:
EmergencyProposalManager can bypass normal governance ONLY if:
1. ThresholdSignatureManager has ≥7 of 9 signatures
2. EmergencyShutdownProtocol is activated
3. Threat is existential (system-wide failure imminent)
4. Action is automatically reversed after 72 hours unless reconfirmed

